S593 dual pigeonhole cap face for C' multiple-of-n rows

PROVED LEMMA
For v=nw, D_v has exactly w caps in each n-clock cell, each of length 2/(n^2 w).
Thus each n-clock cell has total cap capacity 2/n^2.
If mu(G(S') cap [r/n,(r+1)/n)) > 2/n^2 for some r, then G(S') is not contained in D_v, so S is loose.

